cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Nayak
    given-names: Bishwaswarup
    affiliation: "Department of Physics, Indian Institute of Science, Bengaluru"
    email: bishwaswarup@iisc.ac.in
title: "Halo Orbits, Invariant Manifolds and L1/L2 Connections in the Earth–Moon CR3BP"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-16
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bishwaswarup/cr3bp-manifoldtransfer"
url: "https://github.com/Bishwaswarup/cr3bp-manifoldtransfer"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  Python pipeline for Earth–Moon libration-point orbits in the circular
  restricted three-body problem: Richardson initial guesses, a Howell
  differential corrector and pseudo-arclength continuation for L1 and L2 halo
  families, invariant-manifold tubes, energy-matched L1 to L2 patches through
  the lunar region, and an Earth-approach map of the interior unstable
  manifold.
keywords:
  - astrodynamics
  - CR3BP
  - halo orbits
  - invariant manifolds
  - Poincaré section
  - low-energy transfer
  - atmospheric entry
  - Earth-Moon
  - trajectory design
